1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,880
Useful electronics sit in drawers because
we don't know what to do with them.

2
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:09,605
I catalog what I own, then say what

3
00:00:09,725 --> 00:00:12,880
I want: my interests, budget, and
experience.

4
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:16,944
Muse Spark proposes projects from what I
have, and

5
00:00:17,064 --> 00:00:20,569
the rules keep only what my inventory
backs.

6
00:00:20,689 --> 00:00:22,880
I choose the tabletop arcade.

7
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:26,407
Each item is committed to one build.

8
00:00:26,527 --> 00:00:31,880
What is missing becomes a Marketplace
search that I run myself.

9
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:38,880
The connection diagram and the layout here
are a concept preview of the next step.

10
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:44,092
The same approach starts the search for a
replacement part for my

11
00:00:44,212 --> 00:00:48,880
old drink mixer, with the questions to ask
before I buy.

12
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:50,656
Orphan Parts Lens.

13
00:00:50,776 --> 00:00:51,880
Find replacements.

14
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:53,104
Discover reuse.

15
00:00:53,224 --> 00:00:54,880
Build something useful.

